policies=[
('finance2017','Finance Act2017: removal of corporate donation cap and party disclosure','2017-03-31',['finance-act-2017-court','bonds-judgment-2024'],['parliament','finance-ministry'],G,'/political','Section154 omitted Companies Act182(1)’s7.5%three-year average-profit cap and replaced party-specific disclosure with a total amount; related amendments enabled electoral bonds. This is the enacted2017 change, subsequently held unconstitutional in specified parts on15February2024.','Union defended formal banking channels, donor privacy and reducing black money; the Court found less restrictive alternatives and Article14/19 violations.','Compare board approval, profits, corporate filing and matched bank instrument for the applicable period; amount/date overlap alone cannot establish quid pro quo.',['Court ruling concerns legal design, not an automatic finding against every donor.'],'2017 statute; specified funding provisions struck down2024'),
('bonds2024','Electoral bonds2024: disclosure remedy and cessation of issuance','2024-02-15',['bonds-judgment-2024'],['supreme-court','sbi','eci'],G,'/political','2024 INSC113 invalidated the scheme and specified secrecy/unlimited-funding amendments; SBI was directed to stop issuing bonds and disclose purchase/encashment information from12April2019 for ECI publication.','The Court balanced donor informational privacy against voters’ right to know; later production orders and serial-number joins must be read separately.','Use exact instrument identity and denomination to match purchaser and encashment; preserve unmatched rows and exclude assumptions of illegal exchange.',['A disclosed lawful contribution is not itself a public-fund disbursement.'],'struck-down scheme; disclosure directions'),
('ibc2016','IBC2016: creditor process, binding plan and recovery accounting','2016-05-28',['ibc-original-2016','bhushan-share-order-2022','ibbi-named'],['parliament','ibbi','nclt'],F,'/debt','The2016 Code created a creditor-initiated resolution mechanism: section7 admission, creditor committee, section30 plan and section31 approval. Bhushan shows SBI’s application reaching an approved transfer to a new owner. Enactment date is not universal commencement.','Creditor recovery must be compared with liquidation and operating value; debt claims, approved plan-realizable value and verified cash receipts differ. An IBC plan is not the same legal event as an accounting write-off or government loan waiver.','Reconcile plan, creditor-wise distribution and bank cash ledger, preserving claim classes and dates; do not subtract a buyer’s equity cheque from total claims to compute public loss.',['Distress and going-concern value can explain compromise; former owners can lose control.'],'historical enactment; specific plan implemented'),
('ibc29a','Section29A: eligibility checks before acquiring distressed assets','2017-11-23',['ibc29a-2018'],['parliament','ibbi'],F,'/debt','Act8of2018, deemed effective23November2017, inserted disqualifications including wilful default, specified NPA/control relationships and connected persons, plus a defined overdue-payment cure. Liquidation sales received a linked restriction.','This is a dated legal version; later statutory exceptions and amendments must be checked for the bid date. No named bidder is declared ineligible from a shared surname or address.','Verify applicant/connected-person ownership, dates of NPA classification, cure evidence and RP/CoC determination from actual bid documents.',['Eligibility criteria can protect creditors while narrowing a distressed auction’s bidder pool.'],'enacted with retrospective commencement'),
('coal2020','Commercial coal2020: end-use liberalisation and revenue-share auction','2020-01-10',['mineral-laws-2020','coal-act-2015','coal-methodology-2025-annex2020','coal-auction-winners-2020'],['parliament','nominated-authority'],C,'/energy','Act2of2020 broadened coal eligibility/end uses, effective10January2020; the final28May2020 methodology used ascending revenue-share bids payable to states and permitted own use, sale and related-party sales. Radhikapur’s actual21%award is a specific implementation.','The government methodology seeks production and competition; the public audit check is benchmark revenue, production and milestones. January2020 discussion-paper terms were not adopted as final.','Test declared volumes/grade/value against National Coal Index/actual-price methodology and royalty statements; require actual receipts before claiming fiscal gain.',['An open statutory auction is a common mechanism; the published winner table includes different corporate bidders.'],'enacted amendment plus final auction order'),
('mmdr2021','MMDR2021: captive sale permission and transferred clearances','2021-03-28',['mmdr-consolidated-2021'],['parliament','mines-ministry'],C,'/resources','Sections8(5)/8A(7A) permit specified captive mines to sell up to50%of annual output after meeting linked end-use needs, subject to SixthSchedule additional payments. Section8B changes the transfer of statutory clearances. Tariff-bid/UMPP coal exception remains material.','These are permissions with conditions, not proof that any operator sold mineral or remitted money. Historic mine-specific lease and latest implementing rules are needed.','Compare permitted end use, annual production, sale invoices, additional-payment receipt and transfer conditions; apply explicit statutory exclusions before counting beneficiaries.',['Selling genuine surplus may improve utilisation without diverting linked-plant supply.'],'historical enacted amendment'),
('ports2021','Major ports2021: market tariffs with concession royalties intact','2021-11-03',['ports-act-2021','ports-commencement-2021','ports-tariff-2021'],['ports-ministry'],P,'/public-works','The Act commenced3November2021;21December guidelines apply prospectively to future PPP agreements. Concessionaires may publish market-based ceiling tariffs, subject to law, while contract royalties and other conditions continue. TICTPL’s2022concession fits the dated scope.','Existing concessions are a separate comparison class. The retained Act lists covered major ports; corporate Kamarajar/Ennore was not automatically joined.','Inspect concession date/regime, published scale of rates, invoices, minimum throughput and royalty ledger; tariff autonomy alone does not establish a giveaway.',['Market pricing can improve competition and responsiveness while preserving landlord payments.'],'commenced Act; prospective tariff guidelines'),
('airports2018','Six-airport PPP design: experience, concentration and fee basis','2018-12-11',['airports-policy'],['aai'],P,'/public-works','The government’s2023parliamentary explanation identifies the2018PPPAC process: no prior airport experience, no cap on airports bid, and per-passenger fee rather than revenue-sharing. Six airports were awarded50year concessions in2020–21. This was procurement design, not a new Act.','Government states the changes sought competition/flexibility and technical/financial capacity was evaluated; demand uncertainty explained not estimating total50year project cost upfront.','Compare eligible/qualified bidders and per-passenger fee bids with demand, termination and revenue ledgers; do not equate concession tenure with a permanent asset sale.',['Opening eligibility can broaden competition even if one bidder ultimately wins multiple airports.'],'retrospectively documented procurement-policy design'),
('green2022','Green open access2022: industrial purchasing routes and later court challenge','2022-06-06',['green-open-access-2022','karnataka-openaccess-analysis'],['power-ministry'],['energy','public-finance'],'/energy','GSR418(E) introduced100kWgreen-access eligibility,15day processing and developer/distribution-licensee procurement routes. Karnataka HC struck down central/state GEOA measures on20December2024, according to retained specialist reporting; KERC replaced its regulations in2025 and a Union appeal was reported.','Prayas records WritAppeal154/2025 admitted and listed23June2025, based on information compiled30April2025. No later appeal disposition was verified here; this card does not assert an uncontested nationwide current entitlement.','Use the operative state regulation, dated court orders, PPA, wheeling/banking agreement and billing-period charges before quantifying a corporate benefit or distribution-company burden.',['The dispute concerns allocation of regulatory power and banking costs; renewable procurement itself is not evidence of impropriety.'],'historical rules; Karnataka invalidation/appeal reported'),
('procurement2020','Local-content procurement2020: eligibility and L1 matching','2020-09-16',['procurement-2020'],['dpiit'],['public-works','capital','public-funds'],'/procurement','Revised Make-in-India order distinguishes ClassI/ClassII suppliers using local content (normally50%/20%) and gives specified ClassI price-matching/quantity preference within20%margin. It changes allocation rules; it does not authorize charging20%more automatically.','Order’s declared aim is domestic production and employment. Historical2020version only; category-specific nodal rules and later revisions must be checked for each tender.','Recompute local content from import values and auditor certification; compare awarded quantity, eligible class and matched L1 price, with exceptions retained.',['A compliant preference may lawfully favour domestic value added; imports or an Indian brand alone do not determine supplier class.'],'historical revised executive order'),
('dap2020','DAP2020: indigenous-content categories and offset exclusions','2020-10-01',['dap-commencement','defence-dap-2020'],['defence-ministry'],['security','capital','public-funds'],'/security','DAP2020 applies from1October2020. Official retained2021version requires50%indigenous content for Indian-IDDM and excludes offsets in ab-initio single-vendor cases including IGA/FMS. A defence purchase and an offset obligation are separate instruments.','Government launch explains higher indigenous content and domestic capability goals; the retained manual includes later updates, so the exact RFP/date governs.','Identify acquisition category/AoN/RFP, base contract price excluding tax, imported content and applicable offset exception before labelling absent offsets a breach.',['Government-to-government or strategic procurement may lawfully use an offset exception.'],'adopted procedure; retained updated version identified'),
('fcra2020','FCRA2020: designated receipt bank, transfer ban and administrative cap','2020-09-29',['fcra-judgment-2022'],['home-ministry','sbi','supreme-court'],['ngo','governance','finance'],'/ngo','The amendment commenced29September2020: foreign contribution must first enter designated SBI NewDelhi account; onward transfer to another person is barred and administrative-expense limit changed50%to20%. NoelHarper2022upheld challenged provisions, permitting Indian passports under section12A.','Union argued traceability and beneficiary use; petitioners argued operational burdens and fundamental-rights infringement. Court’s conclusion upholds sections7,12(1A),12A,17; expense-cap discussion is context.','Reconcile donor remittance, designated FCRA account, recipient’s utilisation accounts and FC4/audited returns. Distinguish internal account transfers and vendor payments from prohibited grants to another person using actual legal records.',['Lawful foreign funding and an SBI account create neither a public subsidy nor proof of diversion.'],'enacted2020; challenged provisions upheld2022')]
for id,title,date,src,agencies,domain,route,summary,response,test,alts,status in policies:
 entity(id+'-instrument',title,'legal-instrument',src,domain,route,summary)
 rel=id+'-implementation';authority=agencies[0]
 edge(rel,authority,id+'-instrument','Dated enactment, adjudication or implementation framework','legal-framework',date,src,domain,route,summary,records=[id],responses=['green-litigation'] if id=='green2022' else [])
 record(id,title,summary,'policy-change',date,src,agencies+[id+'-instrument'],[rel],domain,route,response,alts,test,status=status,asof='2025-04-30' if id=='green2022' else date,limits=['Curated policy history, not a complete consolidation or a causal finding about an unnamed beneficiary.','Public-interest audit test: '+test])

