record('radhikapur-response','Radhikapur: disputed clearances, alternative remedy and2026cross-appeals','Vedanta cited changed mine boundaries, forest/compensatory-afforestation issues and force majeure. Ministry disputed delay justification. On 2 December 2025 Delhi HC referred the PBG dispute to the CMSP Tribunal and reserved merits. The reported 10 April 2026 cross-appeals instead concerned ST31/2025 and SCN-III proposing termination; both were dismissed with limited protection on that separate track.','response','2026-04-10',['vedanta-judgment-2025-pdf','vedanta-appeal-2026-mirror','vedanta-appeal-pronouncement-2026'],['vedanta-limited','nominated-authority','radhikapur-cmdpa'],[],C+['justice'],'/energy','The original 2025 PBG order continued status quo for ten days or until the tribunal was approached, whichever earlier. The 2026 mirror reports a December 2025 LPA759/2025 extension pending the ST28/2025 stay application; its final outcome remains unverified. April 2026 protection concerns termination notice SCN-III/ST31/2025, not a final determination of PBG recovery. No company contact was attempted; public pleadings supply its position.',['Government enforcement is evidence of a contested contract administration process, not proof of completed cancellation or an improper award.'],'Official2026judgment and laterTalcherTribunal/OrissaHighCourt/SCorders, plus bank debit/state credit confirmation, would settle remaining status.',tier='reported',status='latest found outcome10April2026; final tribunal and cash endpoint unknown',g=cg,limits=['Official2026pronouncement list validates parties/case/date only; substantive2026reasoning remains mirror-reported.'])
