record('tict-response','TICTPL: commercial rationale, minimum throughput and financial-stage limits','Government describes added capacity and lower logistics costs. CARE identifies minimum throughput, royalty, competition, DSCR 1.50 and cash restrictions; its 2024 parent demerger was pending. Government recorded inauguration on 16 September 2024.','response','2024-09-16',['port-inauguration-2024','tict-care-2024'],['voc-port','tictpl','jmbaxi-pl'],[],P,'/public-works','No adverse court proceeding against this concession was verified; no alleged wrongdoing or fabricated denial is introduced. CARE’s risk and obligation record and the government rationale supply counter-evidence. No outreach was attempted.',['Prospective tariff autonomy coexists with royalty and traffic risk; the ₹1 annual licence alone is a misleading valuation.','PSA Sical berth 7 and its litigation are separate and cannot be assigned to TICTPL berth 9.'],'Executed or amended concession, audited royalty receipts and later ownership completion filings would change financial and status inferences.',tier='reported',status='operational announcement verified; latest finance/ownership source September 2024',g=pg)
record('tict-policy-concession','Tuticorin berth 9: new port law → public board → TICTPL → royalty','The 2021 major-port framework applies to the 3 September 2022 VOC–TICTPL DBFOT concession. Government estimated ₹434.17 crore private development; CARE later reports ₹1,900.44 per TEU royalty plus ₹1 annual licence, a 30-year term from 6 April 2023 and ₹482.41 crore long-term / ₹35 crore short-term rated facilities. Terminal inaugurated 16 September 2024.','investigation-case','2022-09-03',['ports-act-2021','ports-commencement-2021','ports-tariff-2021','port-concession-2022','tict-care-2024','port-inauguration-2024','port-ipa-location'],['ports2021-instrument','voc-port','tict-concession','tictpl','jmbaxi-pl'],['port-law-board','voc-tict-concession','tict-concession-spv','jmbaxi-tict','tict-royalty-port','voc-tict-operation'],P,'/public-works','Response card retains government rationale, minimum throughput and debt safeguards. CARE’s royalty and ownership details are reported; full signed concession and actual public royalty receipts remain unobtained.',['Estimated project cost, rated bank limits and royalty rates are incompatible accounting units; differences do not establish a cost overrun or cash transfer.','Old port concessions and specific new SPVs are controls against misapplying prospective 2021 law.'],'Obtain the full concession, post-opening tariffs, volume/royalty statements, port credit entries and latest SPV shareholding before quantifying public receipts or current ownership.',[amount(434.17,'crore','official estimated concessionaire project cost; not state grant','2022-09-03'),amount(482.41,'crore','CARE-rated long-term bank facilities; not verified drawdown','2024-09-05'),amount(35,'crore','CARE-rated short-term bank facilities; not verified drawdown','2024-09-05'),amount(1900.44,'rupees per TEU','reported contractual royalty rate; not total concession value','2024-09-05')],asof='2024-09-16',status='inauguration verified; royalty payments and later ownership not verified',g=pg,limits=['Direct ownership and financial terms retained at the 2024 snapshot; do not treat the pending demerger as completed.','Official port marker describes public authority location, not berth 9 coordinates.'],period='Act commenced 3 November 2021; guidelines 21 December 2021; agreement signed 3 September 2022; CARE start 6 April 2023; rating 5 September 2024; inauguration 16 September 2024')

